  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I wasn't able to perform a sanity build (mvn clean install) in Windows 10 due to some integration tests in fcrepo-kernel-modeshape failing.  A few of them were failing because the last modified date for binaries was not updating all of the time (tests were flapping).  This seems to affect only non-hyper-visor based windows install. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
        "text": "@Ben Pennell"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": ",  ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
        "text": "@Aaron Birkland"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "557058:cc6016b1-6dae-4b52-922c-9076d2e8b96d",
        "text": "@Yinlin Chen"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " have wrestled with the issue.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
